    "text": "96\n\n When a Deal Dies at the 50-Yard Line\nHi Sara,\nI\u2019m in the middle of my busiest season ever, and this week, three deals died.\nAll three had cleared diligence. Purchase agreements were drafted. We were basically at the 50-yard line\u2026and then, poof.\nIf you\u2019ve ever made it that far and still watched a deal fall apart, you know how brutal it is.\u00a0\nHere\u2019s what kills deals that are THIS close to closing:\n1. A surprise pops up\n\nThink lawsuit, data breach, or a key employee walking out.\nIt might not even be a big deal, just bad timing. When something hits late, there\u2019s no time to get clarity. Buyers bail. Solid reps and warranties can save you here by forcing disclosure upfront.\n2. Overlawyering\n\nA $300K asset purchase does not need a 90-page agreement.\nIf your legal team has no business sense, the deal can stall out fast. Sellers walk. Buyers burn out. And you\u2019re left with redlines and regrets.\u00a0\nA good lawyer should help you close, not just edit.\n3. Last-minute deal breaker\n\nEven with a solid LOI, big terms sometimes surface late, like indemnity or personal guarantees.\nIf the gap\u2019s too big and no one will move, the deal\u2019s done. Painful, but better now than post-close.\nWant more real talk about how deals get done\u2014or don\u2019t?\n\nI share weekly insights from the front lines. And if you missed this week\u2019s video, it\u2019s live now on YouTube.\nTo fewer landmines,\nSara Sharp\nDeal Attorney & Founder of Deal Academy\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
